-- NEXUS investigation rebuild, stage 5 of 5: the Avalanche.
--
-- The finale is an evidence chain, not a keypad. P30-P36 are deducted from the
-- stage 5 instruments - the spire console, the memory array, the GM key panel,
-- the failsafe panel, the central hub, the chamber, the observation deck - and
-- only the Operator ever enters a conclusion. P37 carries the team's own
-- disposition as a multi-answer gate; the accepted dispositions are installed by
-- a separate additive migration (2026100609_finale_dispositions.sql) so this file
-- stays a pure function of the design and the disposition update can be read on
-- its own. Each statement below is one puzzle_nodes row, and the wiring that the
-- seed established (nextQrNode, nextPhysicalLocation, evidence id, puzzle type)
-- is preserved untouched: only content, answer_metadata and metadata change.
--
-- P37's answer_metadata intentionally carries a sentinel acceptedAnswer here; the
-- servable answer lives only in 2026100609.

-- P30 The Transmitter Spire - Stage 5
UPDATE puzzle_nodes SET
  content = '{"observer":{"role":"OBSERVER","screenTitle":"Spire Control Console - Slot Board","dataPayload":"SPIRE CONTROL CONSOLE, rooftop transmitter: a board of twenty-eight answer slots. TWENTY-EIGHT ARE LIT. ONE ADDITIONAL SOCKET BESIDE THEM IS DARK and carries no label - the engineer note taped to the board says the socket is not for an answer, it is for the thing that makes answers travel. Below the board, an oscillograph prints three interleaved traces, each from one of the three field handsets, each beating at its own rate until the console locates a common rhythm that none of them holds alone.","visualType":"telemetry","whatTheySee":"A board of twenty-eight lit slots, one unlabelled dark socket, and an oscillograph showing three handset traces converging on one rhythm.","taskPrompt":"Record the state of the board, the dark socket, and the three traces exactly, including their individual rates.","intermediateOutput":"Twenty-eight lit slots, one dark socket with no label, and three traces that only share a rhythm when the console reads them together."},"analyst":{"role":"ANALYST","screenTitle":"Oscillograph - One Rhythm, Three Sources","dataPayload":"OSCILLOGRAPH ANALYSIS: the three traces are not noise. Each handset beats at its own rate; when the console overlays them, the overlay is steady and the individual traces are not. The engineer note calls the socket the carrier, not the payload: it is the thing the twenty-eight answers ride on, and it has three sources and no single source. The note refuses to name the carrier, but the oscillograph is unambiguous about what a recurring beat that travels is called. Whatever you name, it must be five letters: the socket is cut to five contacts.","visualType":"document-forensics","whatTheySee":"An overlay showing one rhythm where three unsteady traces meet, and the engineer note defining the socket as a carrier with three sources.","taskPrompt":"Read the overlay and the note, then decide what kind of thing a recurring beat that travels is called.","intermediateOutput":"The dark socket carries three sources and no single source; the thing it carries is a five-letter recurring beat."},"operator":{"role":"OPERATOR","screenTitle":"Spire Power Coupler - Carrier Field","dataPayload":"SPIRE POWER COUPLER: CARRIER: [ _ _ _ _ _ ]. The coupler throws the dark socket live only when it is told what the socket carries - the five-letter name of the thing the three handset traces share when they are overlaid. The twenty-eight answers on the board stay lit; the socket stays dark until the field is filled.","visualType":"terminal","whatTheySee":"A five-letter carrier field on the coupler, the twenty-eight lit slots above it, and the dark socket beside them.","taskPrompt":"Submit the five-letter name of the carrier the dark socket takes.","intermediateOutput":"Awaiting the team conclusion."},"operatorInvestigation":{"operatorOwnEvidence":"The spire power coupler and its five-letter carrier field, the board of twenty-eight lit slots with one dark unlabelled socket, and the oscillograph overlay of three handset traces.","operatorTaskDescription":"The Observer records the board and the three traces; the Analyst overlays the traces and reads the engineer note to identify what the unlabelled socket carries; the Operator fills the carrier field and throws the socket live.","requiredDiscoveries":{"observerDiscovery":"Records the twenty-eight lit slots, the unlabelled dark socket, and the three individual trace rates.","analystDiscovery":"Overlays the three traces into one rhythm and reads the note to classify the socket as a carrier with three sources of five letters."}},"coordinationChain":{"observerProduces":"Observer reports the board state and the three handset trace rates.","analystTransforms":"Analyst overlays the traces and identifies the carrier the dark socket takes.","operatorExecutes":"Operator submits the five-letter carrier name, unlocking P31."},"hints":["The board is already full - twenty-eight lit slots. The dark socket is the only thing left, and the note says it is not for an answer but for what the answers travel on.","Each handset beats at its own rate; the overlay is steady where the individual traces are not. A recurring beat that travels has a name that fits a five-contact socket.","The engineer note calls the socket a carrier with three sources; give the coupler the five-letter word for that recurring beat and the socket will go live."],"narrativeObjective":"Fill the one socket the answers cannot fill: name the carrier that makes the array answer back.","roleDependencyLevel":"D4"}',
  answer_metadata = '{"acceptedAnswer":"PULSE","validationMethod":"case_insensitive","fullSolution":"The spire board has twenty-eight lit slots and one unlabelled dark socket, which the engineer note defines as a carrier with three sources and no single source. The oscillograph overlays three individual handset traces into one steady rhythm. A recurring beat that travels is a PULSE, five letters, and the socket is cut to five contacts."}',
  metadata = '{"type":"MEMORY","difficulty":4,"time":"9m","storyReveal":"The spire hums: twenty-nine of twenty-eight. The array was never waiting for another answer. It was waiting for the beat that carries the three of you.","locationClue":{"format":"Research-Note","clueText":"LINA''S NOTE: \"Descend to the Nexus Core basement. The memory cylinder array awaits.\"","solution":"Nexus Core Memory Arrays","nextPhysicalLocation":"[NEXUS CORE] - Memory Arrays","nextQrNode":"QR-NODE-31","explanation":"Points to memory arrays."},"evidenceUnlocked":{"id":"EVID-P30","category":"Audio","title":"Dictaphone Memo REC-22: Synchronization","state":"RECOVERED","timestamp":"Stage 5","source":"Spire control console","content":"All twenty-eight answers are in the array, but the array will not answer back until it is given the beat that carries them. The carrier is not another answer. It comes from the three of you, and it is the reason the last socket was left dark."},"whyTeamworkMatters":"Only the observer can read the board and the three trace rates; only the analyst can overlay them into one rhythm and classify the socket; only the operator can fill the carrier field.","feeds":"M04"}'
WHERE code = 'P30';

-- P31 The Memory Array - NOTE ON DESIGN DEVIATION
-- The seed gate for P31 hands the team a multiple-choice recall question about an
-- early answer and asks them to submit SYNC - the answer is a word the gate never
-- evidences, and the only inference is "teams align memories". That fails bible
-- rule 3 (competing hypotheses live in the material) and rule 7 (the gate must
-- advance the case). The rebuild keeps the token and the type but re-scopes the
-- incident as bible section 9 intends: the array is not storage, it is occupied,
-- and the gate is the team's first look at the residents. The four-letter command
-- names the act of reading three traces against one another until they agree.
UPDATE puzzle_nodes SET
  content = '{"observer":{"role":"OBSERVER","screenTitle":"Memory Array - Occupancy Meter","dataPayload":"NEXUS CORE memory array, basement: a rack of cylinders behind a vault door. The vault is sealed; the occupancy meter beside it is NOT at zero. It reads a low, steady figure and it does not fall. A maintenance card on the rack reads: THESE CYLINDERS WERE ORDERED AS BLANK MEDIA. THE METER SAYS OTHERWISE. Three meter taps run from the array to the vault door, one for each field handset; the door reports its own state only when all three taps agree.","visualType":"telemetry","whatTheySee":"A sealed array with a non-zero occupancy meter and three handset taps meeting at the vault door.","taskPrompt":"Record the maintenance card, the meter reading, and the state of all three vault taps exactly.","intermediateOutput":"Cylinders ordered blank, a meter that is not at zero, and three taps that must agree before the door reports."},"analyst":{"role":"ANALYST","screenTitle":"Record Comparison - Blank Media, Occupied Rack","dataPayload":"RECORD COMPARISON: the order card shows the cylinders arriving blank. The meter shows them occupied. Both records are authentic, so the difference is not a filing error: whatever the meter is measuring was not shipped in the cylinders - it was written into them, and it does not decay. The vault will not open on a single reading. Its manual says the door opens only when the three taps report the SAME state in the same instant; a tap that disagrees holds the door, and a tap that lags holds the door. The act the manual names is four letters, and it is the opposite of letting three clocks drift.","visualType":"document-forensics","whatTheySee":"A side-by-side of the blank-media order and the occupied meter, with the vault manual open to its same-instant rule.","taskPrompt":"Reconcile the two records and read the door manual to name the act the door requires.","intermediateOutput":"The archive is occupied by something written after delivery; the door opens on a four-letter act in which all three taps report the same state at once."},"operator":{"role":"OPERATOR","screenTitle":"Vault Door - Command Field","dataPayload":"MEMORY ARRAY VAULT DOOR: COMMAND: [ _ _ _ _ ]. The manual is reproduced above the field. The door will not take a reading from any one tap; it takes the four-letter name of the act it performs when the three taps are brought to the same state at the same instant.","visualType":"terminal","whatTheySee":"A four-letter command field on the vault door, with the manual and the three tap states above it.","taskPrompt":"Submit the four-letter act the door manual requires.","intermediateOutput":"Awaiting the team conclusion."},"operatorInvestigation":{"operatorOwnEvidence":"The vault door command field, the three handset tap states, the non-zero occupancy meter, and the blank-media maintenance card.","operatorTaskDescription":"The Observer records the meter, the card and the three taps; the Analyst reconciles the two records and reads the door manual to name the required act; the Operator submits the four-letter command.","requiredDiscoveries":{"observerDiscovery":"Records the non-zero meter, the blank-media order card, and all three tap states without assuming the door will open.","analystDiscovery":"Reconciles blank media with an occupied meter and identifies the four-letter act of bringing three readings to the same state at once."}},"coordinationChain":{"observerProduces":"Observer reports the occupancy meter, the maintenance card and the three tap states.","analystTransforms":"Analyst reconciles the two records and names the act the door manual requires.","operatorExecutes":"Operator submits the four-letter command, opening the memory array."},"hints":["Two records describe the same rack: an order for blank cylinders, and a meter that will not read zero. Neither record is forged - the meter is measuring something the order never shipped.","The vault manual will not accept a reading from one tap. It opens only when all three taps report the same state in the same instant; something that lags holds the door just as firmly as something that disagrees.","Name the four-letter act of holding three traces to one another until all three agree at once. It is the opposite of letting them drift apart."],"narrativeObjective":"Open the archive by reconciling what was ordered against what is now stored in it.","roleDependencyLevel":"D4"}',
  answer_metadata = '{"acceptedAnswer":"SYNC","validationMethod":"exact","fullSolution":"The maintenance card says the cylinders were ordered as blank media, but the occupancy meter reads non-zero and does not fall: the array is occupied by material written after delivery, and the two authentic records disagree, so the difference is the evidence. The vault manual opens the door only when all three handset taps report the same state at the same instant - a tap that lags holds it as firmly as a tap that disagrees. The four-letter act of bringing the three to one state at once is SYNC."}',
  metadata = '{"type":"MEMORY","difficulty":4,"time":"9m","storyReveal":"The vault answers: MEMORY BANKS ALIGNED. ACCESS GRANTED TO FINAL VAULT. The cylinders that arrived blank are not blank, and whatever was written into them has been waiting for the team to read it together.","locationClue":{"format":"Research-Note","clueText":"LINA''S NOTE: \"Enter the Final Vault. The GM key awaits.\"","solution":"Final Transmission Vault","nextPhysicalLocation":"[NEXUS CORE] - Final Vault","nextQrNode":"QR-NODE-32","explanation":"Points to the final vault."},"evidenceUnlocked":{"id":"EVID-P31","category":"Lab Note","title":"Lab Notebook Fragment #81","state":"RECOVERED","timestamp":"Stage 5","source":"Memory array terminal","content":"The alignment worked, and the GM key is accessible. The array was never storage: it is occupied, and it will only answer when all three of us read it at the same instant. Whatever is left here can only be stopped if all three of us act at the same instant."},"whyTeamworkMatters":"Only the observer can read the meter, the card and the taps; only the analyst can reconcile the two records and read the manual; only the operator can open the door. A team that cannot align three readings cannot pass the vault at all.","feeds":"P30"}'
WHERE code = 'P31';

-- P32 The Three Phones II - Stage 5
UPDATE puzzle_nodes SET
  content = '{"observer":{"role":"OBSERVER","screenTitle":"GM Key Panel - Observer Phone Shard","dataPayload":"THREE PHONE SHARDS at the GM key panel, each handset holding one line of a GM message. OBSERVER SHARD: THE OBSERVER SEES EVERY PATH BUT WALKS NONE ALONE. Under the shard, the panel prints its legend: GM KEY, FIVE LETTERS - THE STATE OF BEING MADE ONE. The observer handset alone shows one line and no sense of what the other two hold.","visualType":"observation","whatTheySee":"One GM message line on the observer handset, plus the panel legend fixing the key at five letters.","taskPrompt":"Record the shard and the panel legend exactly, then communicate the line without guessing the other two.","intermediateOutput":"One shard line and a legend fixing the key at five letters."},"analyst":{"role":"ANALYST","screenTitle":"GM Key Panel - Analyst Phone Shard","dataPayload":"ANALYST SHARD: THE ANALYST BINDS WHAT IS SEEN AND WHAT IS NOT SEEN INTO ONE WORD. The panel legend is the same on every handset and it settles a contradiction the archive left standing: an older memo said the key was seven letters, but the panel is cut to five contacts and the legend reads five. The memo was wrong; the panel is the instrument. Neither this shard nor the observer shard is a definition on its own - each line describes one role''s work, and the three together describe one state.","visualType":"document-forensics","whatTheySee":"A second shard line, the same five-letter legend, and an older memo contradicted by the panel itself.","taskPrompt":"Record the second shard and reject the stale memo in favour of the panel legend.","intermediateOutput":"Two of three shard lines; the key is five letters, not seven."},"operator":{"role":"OPERATOR","screenTitle":"GM Key Panel - Operator Shard and Synthesis","dataPayload":"OPERATOR SHARD: THE OPERATOR ACTS, AND IN ACTING BECOMES THE THIRD OF ONE. COMBINED KEY: [ _ _ _ _ _ ]. The panel takes the five-letter name of the state the three shard lines describe: one who sees, one who binds, one who acts, made into a single thing. The key is cut to five contacts, matching the legend.","visualType":"terminal","whatTheySee":"The third shard line and a five-contact key field on the panel.","taskPrompt":"Combine the three shard lines and submit the five-letter key.","intermediateOutput":"Awaiting the team conclusion."},"operatorInvestigation":{"operatorOwnEvidence":"The GM key panel with its five-contact field and legend, the operator shard line, and the two shard lines reported by the other handsets.","operatorTaskDescription":"The Observer and Analyst report their shard lines; the Analyst also rejects the stale seven-letter memo against the panel legend; the Operator assembles the three lines into the five-letter key and submits it.","requiredDiscoveries":{"observerDiscovery":"Reports the observer shard line and the five-letter panel legend.","analystDiscovery":"Reports the analyst shard line and rejects the stale memo, establishing that the key is five letters not seven."}},"coordinationChain":{"observerProduces":"Observer reports the first GM shard line and the panel legend.","analystTransforms":"Analyst reports the second shard, rejects the stale memo, and fixes the key at five letters.","operatorExecutes":"Operator reports the third shard, assembles all three, and submits the five-letter key, unlocking P33."},"hints":["Three handsets hold three lines, and the panel legend is printed on all three - read it before anything else: it is the only statement in the room about how long the key is.","An older memo claims a longer key. The panel is cut to five contacts and the legend says five letters, so the memo is stale and the instrument is right.","Each shard line describes what one role does. The legend asks for the state of being made one, and the three lines together describe exactly that state. Assemble the five-letter name."],"narrativeObjective":"Assemble one GM key from three role shards, and trust the panel over a stale memo.","roleDependencyLevel":"D4"}',
  answer_metadata = '{"acceptedAnswer":"UNITY","validationMethod":"case_insensitive","fullSolution":"Each handset holds one GM shard line - one who sees, one who binds, one who acts - and the panel legend is printed on all three, fixing the key at five letters over an older seven-letter memo. The state the three lines describe, made into one, is UNITY, five letters, matching the five contacts the panel is cut to."}',
  metadata = '{"type":"THREE_PHONE","difficulty":4,"time":"9m","storyReveal":"The GM speaks: the system cannot be brought down by one hand. It requires the three roles as one, and it says so in the same language on all three handsets.","locationClue":{"format":"Research-Note","clueText":"GM NOTE: \"The GM key is five letters. Enter it to proceed.\"","solution":"GM Key Panel","nextPhysicalLocation":"[NEXUS CORE] - GM Key Panel","nextQrNode":"QR-NODE-33","explanation":"Points to GM key panel."},"evidenceUnlocked":{"id":"EVID-P32","category":"Audio","title":"Dictaphone Memo REC-24: The GM Key","state":"RECOVERED","timestamp":"Stage 5","source":"Vault holographic projector","content":"The three shards combined speak of a single state. The memo calling the key longer than five letters is stale - the panel is cut to five contacts and its legend says five. Whatever the key names, it is something neither one role nor one handset can hold."},"whyTeamworkMatters":"No handset can see the other two shards, and the stale memo can only be refuted by someone holding the panel legend. The gate cannot be passed by one role reading aloud.","feeds":"P31"}'
WHERE code = 'P32';

-- P33 The GM Key Protocol - Stage 5
UPDATE puzzle_nodes SET
  content = '{"observer":{"role":"OBSERVER","screenTitle":"Final Vault - Failsafe Panel","dataPayload":"GM KEY PANEL, final vault: a seven-contact key field, and beside it a panel the seed memo called the final protocol. The panel is stamped FAILSAFE and it arms on one condition printed in full: WHEN EVERY STREAM ARRIVES AT ONE POINT AT ONE INSTANT. Three stream indicators sit under the stamp, one per role, each showing where that stream currently terminates. The panel is wired to nothing that can be switched off; it has no off position at all.","visualType":"observation","whatTheySee":"A stamped failsafe panel with three stream indicators and no off position, beside a seven-contact key field.","taskPrompt":"Record the stamp, the arming condition and all three stream terminations exactly.","intermediateOutput":"A failsafe that arms only when all three streams arrive at one point at one instant, with no way to disable it."},"analyst":{"role":"ANALYST","screenTitle":"Panel Reading - Failsafe, Not Override","dataPayload":"PANEL READING: the vault has two panels that are easy to confuse. One is an override: it has an off position and it can stop a machine. This one does not; the stamp reads FAILSAFE, and a failsafe is not a switch that stops a system, it is a condition the system reaches on its own. The condition is printed plainly - every stream arrives at one point at one instant - and the three indicators show three streams that currently terminate in three different places. When they terminate together, the panel arms by itself. The memo never names the act; it only defines the condition. Seven contacts, seven letters: the verb for what the three streams do when they meet at one point at one instant.","visualType":"document-forensics","whatTheySee":"A reading that separates an override with an off position from a failsafe that arms on a condition, applied to three diverging streams.","taskPrompt":"Decide which panel this is and derive the seven-letter verb for what the streams must do.","intermediateOutput":"It is a failsafe, not an override; it arms when three streams meet at one point at one instant; the act is seven letters."},"operator":{"role":"OPERATOR","screenTitle":"Failsafe Panel - Arming Field","dataPayload":"FAILSAFE PANEL: ARMING FIELD: [ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ ]. The field takes the seven-letter verb the memo defines - what the three streams do when they arrive at one point at one instant. The three stream indicators above the field still show three separate terminations.","visualType":"terminal","whatTheySee":"A seven-letter arming field under three stream indicators that still diverge.","taskPrompt":"Submit the seven-letter verb the failsafe definition implies.","intermediateOutput":"Awaiting the team conclusion."},"operatorInvestigation":{"operatorOwnEvidence":"The failsafe panel and its seven-letter arming field, the panel stamp, the printed arming condition, and the three stream indicators.","operatorTaskDescription":"The Observer records the stamp and the three terminations; the Analyst distinguishes the failsafe from an override and derives the seven-letter act from the printed condition; the Operator submits it.","requiredDiscoveries":{"observerDiscovery":"Records the FAILSAFE stamp, the arming condition verbatim, and the three separate stream terminations.","analystDiscovery":"Separates a failsafe that arms on a condition from an override with an off position, and derives the seven-letter act from the condition."}},"coordinationChain":{"observerProduces":"Observer reports the stamp, the arming condition and the three stream terminations.","analystTransforms":"Analyst rejects the override reading and derives the seven-letter act from the printed condition.","operatorExecutes":"Operator submits the seven-letter verb, arming the panel and unlocking P34."},"hints":["The word PROTOCOL on the old memo made everyone in this vault look for a switch. Check the panel itself: does it have an off position, or is it stamped as a condition the system reaches?","A failsafe is not something you throw; it is a state the system arrives at. The printed condition says exactly how: every stream reaches ONE POINT at ONE INSTANT, and the three indicators show that has not happened yet.","Take the condition literally and find the seven-letter verb for what three separate streams do when they arrive at one point at one instant. The panel is cut to seven contacts."],"narrativeObjective":"Read the finale correctly: this is a failsafe the system arms itself with, not an override the team can throw.","roleDependencyLevel":"D4"}',
  answer_metadata = '{"acceptedAnswer":"CONVERGE","validationMethod":"case_insensitive","fullSolution":"The panel is stamped FAILSAFE, not override: it has no off position and it arms on the condition printed in full - when every stream arrives at one point at one instant. The three indicators show three streams terminating in three places, so the condition is not yet met. The seven-letter verb for what the streams do when they meet at one point at one instant is CONVERGE; the field is cut to seven contacts."}',
  metadata = '{"type":"DEDUCTION","difficulty":4.5,"time":"8m","storyReveal":"The panel prints: ARMED. FINAL STAGE INITIATED. There was never a switch here. The three of you are the switch, and the vault only works when all three streams arrive together.","locationClue":{"format":"Poetic","clueText":"LINA''S NOTE: \"Enter the Nexus Core central hub. The final truth awaits.\"","solution":"Nexus Core Central Hub","nextPhysicalLocation":"[NEXUS CORE] - Central Hub","nextQrNode":"QR-NODE-34","explanation":"Points to central hub for the final puzzles."},"evidenceUnlocked":{"id":"EVID-P33","category":"Classified","title":"Classified Memo: Final Protocol","state":"RECOVERED","timestamp":"Stage 5","source":"GM Key terminal","content":"GM PROTOCOL: the panel requires all three streams to arrive at one point at one instant. No single role can arm it, and there is no switch to throw - the condition is the team meeting, and nothing else."},"whyTeamworkMatters":"Only the observer can read the stamp and the three terminations; only the analyst can reject the override reading and derive the act; only the operator can arm the panel. Deriving, not throwing, is the whole gate.","feeds":"P32"}'
WHERE code = 'P33';

-- P34 The Final Sequence - Stage 5
UPDATE puzzle_nodes SET
  content = '{"observer":{"role":"OBSERVER","screenTitle":"Central Hub - Sequence Viewer","dataPayload":"CENTRAL HUB SEQUENCE REEL, twelve frames numbered one to twelve. Frames one, two, three, five, six, seven, nine and ten read A, B, C, E, F, G, I, J. Two frames are blank: FRAME FOUR and FRAME EIGHT. Both blanks are struck through with a single red line. A plate under the reel reads: THE FIRST APPLIED VALUE IS THE INITIATOR. The reel turns on its own; nothing on this screen asks you to stop it.","visualType":"observation","whatTheySee":"A twelve-frame reel with frames four and eight blank and struck through, and a plate pointing at the first applied value.","taskPrompt":"Record every frame value, both blank frames, and the plate exactly.","intermediateOutput":"Eight letters recorded, frames four and eight blank, and a plate naming the first applied value as the initiator."},"analyst":{"role":"ANALYST","screenTitle":"Pattern Analyzer - First Missing","dataPayload":"PATTERN ANALYSIS: the eight printed frames advance by one letter each and skip nothing - A, B, C, then a gap, then E, F, G, then a gap, then I, J. The gaps are the two omitted positions in a plain alphabet run: position four and position eight. The hub plate says only the FIRST applied value initiates, so the second gap is never submitted and the reel is already turning without it. The protocol takes the first omitted value as a single letter.","visualType":"document-forensics","whatTheySee":"An analyzer showing a plain alphabet run with two omissions and a plate restricting the protocol to the first.","taskPrompt":"Identify both omissions, then determine which one the protocol takes.","intermediateOutput":"Two omissions at positions four and eight; the protocol takes the first as a single letter."},"operator":{"role":"OPERATOR","screenTitle":"Protocol Initiator - Sequence Field","dataPayload":"PROTOCOL INITIATOR: INITIATE: [ _ ]. The field takes one letter - the first applied value from the sequence reel, per the plate. The reel continues to turn above the field; the hub does not stop for a second value.","visualType":"terminal","whatTheySee":"A single-letter initiation field beneath a turning sequence reel.","taskPrompt":"Submit the single-letter initiation value.","intermediateOutput":"Awaiting the team conclusion."},"operatorInvestigation":{"operatorOwnEvidence":"The protocol initiator and its single-letter field, the twelve-frame sequence reel with two struck blanks, and the hub plate naming the first applied value as the initiator.","operatorTaskDescription":"The Observer records the reel; the Analyst finds both omissions and applies the plate to choose the first; the Operator submits the single letter.","requiredDiscoveries":{"observerDiscovery":"Records the eight printed frames, both struck blanks, and the plate verbatim.","analystDiscovery":"Locates both omitted positions in the alphabet run and reads the plate to select the first omission only."}},"coordinationChain":{"observerProduces":"Observer reports the reel, both blanks and the plate.","analystTransforms":"Analyst identifies the two omissions and selects the first per the plate.","operatorExecutes":"Operator submits the single first value, unlocking P35."},"hints":["The reel is not a cipher. Read the printed letters in order and notice what kind of run they are making.","There are two blanks, not one, and the plate tells you that only the FIRST applied value acts as the initiator. Do not submit the second.","Fill in the missing letter at the earlier of the two blank frames - the position that comes right after the third printed value - and submit that single letter."],"narrativeObjective":"Read the sequence correctly and take only the first value the protocol applies.","roleDependencyLevel":"D4"}',
  answer_metadata = '{"acceptedAnswer":"D","validationMethod":"exact","fullSolution":"The eight printed frames run A, B, C, E, F, G, I, J: a plain alphabet run with two omissions, at position four and position eight. The hub plate says only the FIRST applied value initiates, so the second omission is not submitted. The first omitted value, the letter that follows C in the run, is D."}',
  metadata = '{"type":"PATTERN","difficulty":4.5,"time":"8m","storyReveal":"The hub prints: SEQUENCE COMPLETE. FINAL ENTITY ENTRY DETECTED. The sequence was already running before anyone touched it - the reel only needed the team to apply its first value and let the rest turn.","locationClue":{"format":"Research-Note","clueText":"LINA''S NOTE: \"The entity awaits. All three must agree to proceed.\"","solution":"Final Boss Chamber","nextPhysicalLocation":"[NEXUS CORE] - Final Boss Chamber","nextQrNode":"QR-NODE-35","explanation":"Points to the final boss chamber."},"evidenceUnlocked":{"id":"EVID-P34","category":"Audio","title":"Dictaphone Memo REC-26: The Entity","state":"RECOVERED","timestamp":"Stage 5","source":"Central hub terminal","content":"The sequence was already turning. It only ever needed the first applied value, and it cannot manifest until all three of us confirm our presence and our choice at one instant."},"whyTeamworkMatters":"Only the observer can read the reel and the plate; only the analyst can locate both omissions and apply the plate; only the operator can apply the single value. A team that submits the second omission stalls the hub.","feeds":"P33"}'
WHERE code = 'P34';

-- P35 The Final Choice - Stage 5
UPDATE puzzle_nodes SET
  content = '{"observer":{"role":"OBSERVER","screenTitle":"Final Boss Chamber - Observer Consent Field","dataPayload":"FINAL BOSS CHAMBER: three consent fields stand on a single console, one per role. The OBSERVER FIELD is live for the observer handset only and reads: CONFIRM YOU WILL PROCEED WITH THE FINAL CHOICE. A rule plate above all three fields reads: EACH FIELD IS SET BY ITS OWN HOLDER. THERE IS NO PROXY. A MAJORITY IS NOT A DECISION. Two of the three fields are currently unset, and the plate is explicit that no other field can be set on their holders'' behalf.","visualType":"observation","whatTheySee":"Three consent fields on one console, one live, and a plate forbidding proxies and majorities.","taskPrompt":"Record the consent fields, the rule plate, and the state of each field exactly.","intermediateOutput":"Three fields, one settable per holder, no proxy and no majority allowed."},"analyst":{"role":"ANALYST","screenTitle":"Consent Ledger - No Proxy, No Majority","dataPayload":"CONSENT LEDGER: the rule plate removes the two shortcuts. A majority is not a decision here - two fields set out of three will not satisfy the console. A proxy is not a decision either - one holder cannot set another''s field, and the ledger records each field against the handset that raised it, not against a name. The console takes the five-letter verb for what three holders do when each sets their own field and all three fields stand at once. It is not COMPLY, which one holder can do alone, and it is not REFUSE, which one holder can also do alone.","visualType":"document-forensics","whatTheySee":"A consent ledger that records fields against handsets, excluding both majority and proxy readings.","taskPrompt":"Rule out the shortcuts, then name the five-letter act three independent holders must perform.","intermediateOutput":"No majority, no proxy; the act is five letters and requires all three holders at once."},"operator":{"role":"OPERATOR","screenTitle":"Consent Console - Initiation Field","dataPayload":"CONSENT CONSOLE: INITIATION: [ _ _ _ _ _ ]. The field takes the five-letter verb for what the three holders do when each field is set by its own holder and no field stands in for another. The three field states are reproduced above it.","visualType":"terminal","whatTheySee":"A five-letter initiation field beneath three separately-held consent fields.","taskPrompt":"Submit the five-letter act the three holders perform.","intermediateOutput":"Awaiting the team conclusion."},"operatorInvestigation":{"operatorOwnEvidence":"The consent console and its five-letter initiation field, the rule plate forbidding proxies and majorities, and the three consent field states.","operatorTaskDescription":"The Observer records the fields and the plate; the Analyst rules out majority and proxy readings in the ledger; the Operator submits the five-letter act that requires all three holders at once.","requiredDiscoveries":{"observerDiscovery":"Records the three consent fields, their holders, and the rule plate verbatim.","analystDiscovery":"Eliminates majority and proxy readings and identifies the five-letter act three independent holders perform together."}},"coordinationChain":{"observerProduces":"Observer reports the three consent fields and the rule plate.","analystTransforms":"Analyst rules out majority and proxy readings against the consent ledger.","operatorExecutes":"Operator submits the five-letter act, unlocking P36."},"hints":["The rule plate closes two doors before you start: a majority is not a decision, and nobody may set a field but its own holder. Whatever the console wants cannot be reached by two of three.","COMPLY can be done by one holder alone, and so can REFUSE. Neither is a decision at this console - both leave the other two fields untouched.","The console asks for a five-letter verb. It is what three separate holders do when each raises their own field and all three fields stand at the same time."],"narrativeObjective":"Make a decision that cannot be made by a majority or by one holder on another''s behalf.","roleDependencyLevel":"D4"}',
  answer_metadata = '{"acceptedAnswer":"AGREE","validationMethod":"case_insensitive","fullSolution":"The rule plate forbids proxies (each field is set by its own holder) and majorities (two of three is not a decision), and the consent ledger records fields against handsets rather than names. COMPLY and REFUSE are both acts a single holder can perform, leaving the other fields unset. The five-letter verb for three separate holders each setting their own consent field at once is AGREE."}',
  metadata = '{"type":"NARRATIVE_INVESTIGATION","difficulty":4.5,"time":"8m","storyReveal":"The entity speaks: NOW YOU ARE READY. PROCEED. The chamber never wanted a majority. It wanted three consents, or none.","locationClue":{"format":"Poetic","clueText":"LINA''S NOTE: \"The GM watches and will now guide you.\"","solution":"GM Observation Deck","nextPhysicalLocation":"[NEXUS CORE] - GM Observation Deck","nextQrNode":"QR-NODE-36","explanation":"Points to GM deck for final stage."},"evidenceUnlocked":{"id":"EVID-P35","category":"Audio","title":"Dictaphone Memo REC-28: The GM","state":"RECOVERED","timestamp":"Stage 5","source":"Final boss chamber","content":"Three consents, or none. The chamber takes each field from its own holder and refuses proxies and majorities. All three of you are recognised as the true candidates now, and the GM is about to show you who has been watching."},"whyTeamworkMatters":"Each field is live only on its own holder''s handset, so a team cannot substitute for one another even if they want to. The gate is the decision itself, and it takes all three.","feeds":"P34"}'
WHERE code = 'P35';

-- P36 The GM Intervention - Stage 5
UPDATE puzzle_nodes SET
  content = '{"observer":{"role":"OBSERVER","screenTitle":"GM Observation Deck - Broadcast Channel","dataPayload":"GM OBSERVATION DECK, broadcast channel: a voice you have heard on every screen since Stage 4 addresses the team directly. CANDIDATE GROUP: you have called this place an institute, a facility, a database and a bunker. Every one of those names was wrong. You have also described what you are doing here, and every one of your descriptions has been about the thing you were doing it to - the file, the exhibits, the levels. The broadcast ends with a single instruction: NAME THE LEVEL YOU ARE STANDING IN. A small engraved plate on the deck railing reads: THE FILE IS AN EXHIBIT.","visualType":"observation","whatTheySee":"A GM broadcast that rejects every physical description of the site, and a railing plate calling the file itself an exhibit.","taskPrompt":"Record the broadcast and the railing plate exactly.","intermediateOutput":"A broadcast rejecting physical descriptions of the site and an instruction to name the level, plus a plate making the file itself an exhibit."},"analyst":{"role":"ANALYST","screenTitle":"Catalogue Card - The Level Names Itself","dataPayload":"CATALOGUE CARD: the railing plate is the whole argument. Every exhibit in this building was catalogued under a class, and the file the team has been carrying is itself an exhibit - catalogued, classed, and shelved among the rest. A catalogue entry for a thing that is about its own catalogue is called the level''s own name, and the class card is cut to FOUR LETTERS. The broadcast is not asking who runs the site. It is asking what the team has been standing inside since the first room.","visualType":"document-forensics","whatTheySee":"A catalogue card classing the case file as an exhibit, with a four-letter class field.","taskPrompt":"Read the railing plate against the catalogue, and name the class the level belongs to.","intermediateOutput":"The file is an exhibit among exhibits; the class for that is four letters and is what the level has been all along."},"operator":{"role":"OPERATOR","screenTitle":"Level Designation - Command Field","dataPayload":"LEVEL DESIGNATION: [ _ _ _ _ ]. The command takes the four-letter class of a level that is about the case the level belongs to. The broadcast and the railing plate are reproduced above the field.","visualType":"terminal","whatTheySee":"A four-letter level designation field beneath the broadcast and the railing plate.","taskPrompt":"Submit the four-letter level designation.","intermediateOutput":"Awaiting the team conclusion."},"operatorInvestigation":{"operatorOwnEvidence":"The level designation field, the GM broadcast rejecting physical descriptions, and the railing plate classing the case file as an exhibit.","operatorTaskDescription":"The Observer records the broadcast and the plate; the Analyst reads the plate against the catalogue to derive the four-letter class; the Operator submits the designation.","requiredDiscoveries":{"observerDiscovery":"Records the broadcast and the railing plate verbatim, including the four-letter class hint.","analystDiscovery":"Recognises the case file as an exhibit among exhibits and derives the four-letter class that names a level about itself."}},"coordinationChain":{"observerProduces":"Observer reports the broadcast and the railing plate.","analystTransforms":"Analyst reads the plate against the catalogue and derives the four-letter class.","operatorExecutes":"Operator submits the level designation, unlocking P37."},"hints":["The broadcast spends its whole length rejecting your names for this place - institute, facility, database, bunker. None of them is what it wants, because none of them concerns the file you are carrying.","Read the railing plate: the case file is itself an exhibit, catalogued and classed like everything else in the building. A level whose exhibit is the level is named by its class.","The catalogue card is cut to four letters. Name the class of a level that is about the case the level belongs to, and enter that single four-letter designation."],"narrativeObjective":"Recognise that the level has been cataloguing the team all along, and name it by its class.","roleDependencyLevel":"D5"}',
  answer_metadata = '{"acceptedAnswer":"META","validationMethod":"exact","fullSolution":"The GM broadcast rejects every physical description of the site and instructs the team to name the level. The railing plate argues the point: the case file is itself an exhibit, catalogued and classed among the rest. A level whose subject is the level itself - a catalogue entry about its own catalogue - is classed META, four letters, the designation the command field is cut to."}',
  metadata = '{"type":"META","difficulty":5,"time":"7m","storyReveal":"The GM broadcast closes: the Bureau was never watching the building. It was cataloguing the team, and the team has been standing inside the exhibit since the first room.","locationClue":{"format":"Poetic","clueText":"GM NOTE: \"The final boss awaits. Only the complete team may enter.\"","solution":"Final Boss Arena","nextPhysicalLocation":"[NEXUS CORE] - Final Boss Arena","nextQrNode":"QR-NODE-37","explanation":"Points to final boss arena."},"evidenceUnlocked":{"id":"EVID-P36","category":"Classified","title":"Classified Memo: Final Boss Protocol","state":"RECOVERED","timestamp":"Stage 5","source":"GM observation deck","content":"GM PROTOCOL: the final room requires the whole team at once. The team has been catalogued since intake, and the last exhibit is the team itself. Whatever happens next is the team''s choice, entered together."},"whyTeamworkMatters":"Only the observer can read the broadcast and the plate; only the analyst can class the level against the catalogue; only the operator can enter the designation. Recognising the team as the exhibit is a shared inference, not a shared password.","feeds":"P35"}'
WHERE code = 'P36';

-- P37 The Final Boss - Stage 5
